[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676383004","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103179#issuecomment-2676383004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103179","id":2676383004,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fhl0c","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T20:32:33Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T20:32:33Z","body":"Confirmed the observed behavior in 4.3 and 4.4rc1.\n\nThis looks like an expected limitation after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94321. In 4.4, meshes used by CSGMesh3D are expected to be [manifold](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/3d/csg_tools.html#custom-meshes). See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100014 for previous discussion of using a quad in CSGMesh3D.\n\nFor just rendering a quad mesh (or any other non-manifold mesh), you should use a MeshInstance3D, not a CSGMesh3D.\n\nHowever, it looks like in your case of setting the mesh at runtime, you don't get any useful errors or node configuration warnings like you do when setting a CSGMesh3D in the editor:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7073fe6b-8d57-46a8-bc8a-b38d1eb2d568)\n\nPerhaps we need some runtime errors or warnings for non-manifoldness?\n\nCC @fire ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676383004/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676390449","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103179#issuecomment-2676390449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103179","id":2676390449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fhnox","user":{"login":"Jools64","id":8512826,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MTI4MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8512826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64","html_url":"https://github.com/Jools64","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jools64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T20:52:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T20:52:11Z","body":"> Confirmed the observed behavior in 4.3 and 4.4rc1.\n> \n> This looks like an expected limitation after [#94321](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94321). In 4.4, meshes used by CSGMesh3D are expected to be [manifold](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/3d/csg_tools.html#custom-meshes). See [#100014](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100014) for previous discussion of using a quad in CSGMesh3D.\n> \n> For just rendering a quad mesh (or any other non-manifold mesh), you should use a MeshInstance3D, not a CSGMesh3D.\n> \n> However, it looks like in your case of setting the mesh at runtime, you don't get any useful errors or node configuration warnings like you do when setting a CSGMesh3D in the editor:\n> \n> ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7073fe6b-8d57-46a8-bc8a-b38d1eb2d568)\n> \n> Perhaps we need some runtime errors or warnings for non-manifoldness?\n> \n> CC [@fire](https://github.com/fire)\n\nAh, I see. Thanks for looking into it. I definitely think runtime error would be helpful.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676390449/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695111774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103179#issuecomment-2695111774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103179","id":2695111774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gpCRe","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/